Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:43:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix react/no-unescaped-entities violations and gate
 deployment on lint

Restores GitHub Pages, which has served a stale build since
2026-10-22T00:51:54Z (head ab8570bf). 45 consecutive Pages runs failed at
"Build static site" with the deploy step skipped, so the public site stayed up
but six days behind.

Escape five apostrophes in JSX text. This is the complete set, confirmed from CI
annotations rather than assumed:

  src/components/site-help.tsx:44              page's      (introduced by 678193d3)
  src/app/page.tsx:6                           What's
  src/app/page.tsx:7                           What's
  src/app/page.tsx:7                           publisher's
  src/app/explore/public-safety/page.tsx:7     homepage's

Rendered output is unchanged: JSX decodes &apos; back to an apostrophe, so
markup, the SEO surface and reader-visible text are all identical.

src/app/mynewspace/page.tsx:68 also contains an apostrophe and is deliberately
left alone. It is a JavaScript template literal inside `export const metadata`,
where an apostrophe is correct; escaping it would corrupt the page title.

Why the workflow change is part of the fix rather than a separate concern:
next.config.ts sets no eslint.eslintDirs, so `next build` lints only Next's
default dirs (app, pages, components). Violations under src/app/ therefore did
NOT fail the Pages build. CI lint went red on src/app/page.tsx and
src/app/explore/public-safety/page.tsx from 2026-10-22T00:48Z onward while Pages
kept deploying successfully; Pages only broke once the same class of violation
landed in src/components/. A red gate that does not gate the artifact being
published is not a gate.

deploy-pages.yml now runs the whole-repo eslint pass between `npm ci` and the
data-sync steps, so a lint violation fails the build before anything is uploaded
or deployed. This matters more than it looks: the workflow runs hourly on cron as
well as on every push to main, so an unlinted commit was being republished every
hour with nobody watching.

Verified before committing: YAML parses; build step order is checkout,
setup-node, npm ci, lint gate, cache, data syncs, configure-pages, build, upload
artifact; deploy retains needs: build and the `github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'`
guard; and removing the inserted block reproduces the original workflow byte for
byte. The five escape sites were each asserted to occur exactly once, and the
edits were verified to change nothing except those apostrophes.

Not verified: no build or lint run was executed, because npm ci for this project
cannot complete in the authoring sandbox. The authoritative check is the Pages
workflow itself turning green on main.
